# Keep the knowledge graph about OUR code.
#
# graphify's built-in skip list covers node_modules, dist, build and its own
# output, but not Composer's vendor/ — so the PHP half of this repo was indexed
# as Laravel framework internals. A 106 MB graph answered "where is the
# clearance two-act split enforced" with Stringable, InvalidArgumentException
# and psysh's readline buffer, which is why the mandatory query hook was being
# ignored: the tool had nothing useful to say.
#
# Everything below is either somebody else's source, generated, or a test
# artefact. None of it is architecturally meaningful for this system.

api/vendor
api/storage
api/bootstrap/cache

web/dist
web/test-results
web/playwright-report
web/.auth

graphify-out
.planning/graphs

# Build outputs and caches that the default list misses in this layout
**/.vite
**/coverage
